event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BU42FD1PVbFDQLommPCLX5", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 8689, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Psg2H1nzfdT3CELWGaQfqE", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 8989, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Psg2H1nzfdT3CELWGaQfqE", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 8989, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Psg2H1nzfdT3CELWGaQfqE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 8989, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SRCLP9kKTaBCLdNeBAikxK", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Follow-up: confirm recovery of error rate and health checks, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 9589, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SRCLP9kKTaBCLdNeBAikxK", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 9589, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SRCLP9kKTaBCLdNeBAikxK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 10986, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\nv2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging, so I skipped both. No change-manager approval was needed because this was a rollback to a previously healthy version.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the follow-up work: confirm recovery and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing. The on-call engineer was paged.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013MJo8W7MPDVJLd7Udsu89r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GA3c9Swn8ms1YXMyVJuyYP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production). Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BU42FD1PVbFDQLommPCLX5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Psg2H1nzfdT3CELWGaQfqE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SRCLP9kKTaBCLdNeBAikxK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Follow-up: confirm recovery of error rate and health checks, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\nv2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging, so I skipped both. No change-manager approval was needed because this was a rollback to a previously healthy version.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the follow-up work: confirm recovery and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing. The on-call engineer was paged.", "type": "text"}]}]}